<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see hot, sunny weather.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see hot, sunny weather.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Thursday were forecast to see mainly sunny skies and hot weather, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see sun in the south and centre and showers in the north with highs of 20 to 30 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see mainly sunny skies with highs around 27 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see a mix of sun and cloud with highs of 25 to 30 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
